carpet -- ideal of a K3 carpet
******************************

  * Usage: 
        I = carpet L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * CoefficientField, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ground field
      * VariableName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientField => ..., default value ZZ/32003
      * VariableName => ..., default value "x"
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

the K3 carpet of type b1,b2 is the correspondence scroll of type b1,b2 with
respect to the ideal Delta^2, where Delta \subset P^1 x P^1 is the ideal of the
diagonal.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : betti res carpet{1,3}|
|                          |
|            0 1 2 3       |
|o1 = total: 1 5 5 1       |
|         0: 1 . . .       |
|         1: . 3 2 .       |
|         2: . 2 3 .       |
|         3: . . . 1       |
|                          |
|o1 : BettiTally           |
+--------------------------+

