correspondencePolynomial -- computes the Hilbert polynomial of a correspondence scroll
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        H = correspondencePolynomial(M,L)
        H = correspondencePolynomial(M,L,VariableName =>h)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of ZZ
      * VariableName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => ..., default value "s"
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in QQ[h]

Description
===========

Let M be a module over a polynomial ring P =
kk[x_{0,0}..x_{0,a_0}..x_{n-1,0}..x_{n-1,a_{n-1}}] graded with degree x_{i,j} =
e_i, the i-th unit vector, and let b = {b_0..b_{n-1}} be a list of integers.
The code computes the multigraded Hilbert polynomial mH(h_0,..,h_{n-1}) and
returns H(h) = mH(b_0*h_0, .., b_{n-1}*h_{n-1}).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = productOfProjectiveSpaces {1,1}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = P                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Delta = smallDiagonal P                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ideal(- x   x    + x   x   )                                            |
|              0,1 1,0    0,0 1,1                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of P                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = P^1/(Delta^2)                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = cokernel | x_(0,1)^2x_(1,0)^2-2x_(0,0)x_(0,1)x_(1,0)x_(1,1)+x_(0,0)^2x_(|
|                                                                             |
|                            1                                                |
|o3 : P-module, quotient of P                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|1,1)^2 |                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : correspondencePolynomial (M,{1,1})                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 4s                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : QQ[s]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : correspondencePolynomial (M,{2,2})                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 8s                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : QQ[s]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

