correspondenceScroll -- Union of planes joining points of rational normal curves according to a given correspondence
********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = correspondenceScroll(I,scroll)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, ideal of a correspondence; an
        arbitrary subscheme of (P^1)^{#scroll}
      * VariableName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, name of the
        variable to use in the output
      * scroll, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of positive integers,
        the degrees of disjoint rational normal curves
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => ..., default value "x"
  * Outputs:
      * G, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, ideal of the generalized
        scroll

Description
===========

Let L = {a_0,..a_{(m-1)}}, and let P = P^N with N = (#L-1+ sum L). Just as the
ordinary scroll S(L) is  the union of planes joining rational normal curves C_i
of degree a_i according to some chosen isomorphism among them (a (1,1,..,1)
correspondence), the generalized Scroll is the union of planes joining the
points that correspond under an arbitrary correspondence, specified by I.

Thus if I is the ideal of the small diagonal of (P^1)^m, then generalized
Scroll(I,L) is equal to S(L). If #L = 2, and I is the square of the ideal of
the diagonal, we get a K3 carpet:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
